# Implementation Plan - Gmail Diet Photo Fetcher

Enable `hirakura10@gmail.com` to receive diet photos and automatically process them.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Gmail App Password Required**: To access Gmail via script, you cannot use your normal login password. You must generate an **"App Password" (アプリパスワード)** from your Google Account settings.
> 1. Go to Google Account > Security > 2-Step Verification.
> 2. Scroll to bottom > App passwords.
> 3. Create one named "DietScript" and copy the 16-character code.

## Proposed Changes

### [scripts]

#### [NEW] [scripts/fetch_gmail_diet.py](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/scripts/fetch_gmail_diet.py)
- **Functionality**:
    - Connects to Gmail (IMAP) using `hirakura10@gmail.com` and the App Password.
    - Searches for **unread** emails with the subject containing **"Diet"** (or specific keyword to avoid processing all spam/personal mail).
    - Downloads image attachments to `C:\Users\hirak\Desktop`.
    - Marks the email as read/archived.
    - **Note**: Once saved to Desktop, the existing `watch_diet.ps1` will automatically pick it up and process it.

#### [MODIFY] [scripts/watch_diet.ps1](file:///c:/Users/hirak/Desktop/2nd-Brain/scripts/watch_diet.ps1)
- **Optional**: Could add a loop to run the python fetcher check every minute, or keep them separate.
- **Decision**: Keep separate or run via Task Scheduler? For simplicity now, I can add a loop in a new batch file that runs both, or just run the python script in a loop.

## Verification Plan

1. User sends an email to `hirakura10@gmail.com` with subject "Diet" and an image attached.
2. Run `scripts/fetch_gmail_diet.py`.
3. Verify image appears on Desktop.
4. Verify `watch_diet.ps1` picks it up and processes it.
